## Reader stories

> ![Neel Nanda]() 
> 
> After earning his maths degree at Cambridge, Neel saw finance and further study as his main options. He'd long been concerned about [AI risks](https://80000hours.org/problem-profiles/artificial-intelligence/), but wasn't sure how to help. A call with our [1-1 team](https://80000hours.org/speak-with-us/?int%5Fcampaign=homepage%5F%5Fneel%5Freader%5Fstory) helped him see AI safety research as a viable option. We connected him to key researchers and helped him secure an internship at Oxford's Future of Humanity Institute, followed by internships at DeepMind and UC Berkeley. These experiences set him on a path to becoming a leading [AI safety technical researcher](https://80000hours.org/career-reviews/ai-safety-researcher/). Neel has since published influential work on mechanistic interpretability and is now a researcher at DeepMind, working to make advanced AI systems more transparent.
